        "block_id": "block_000058",
        "block_index": 58,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trying to conceive can sometimes feel like you’re back in chemistry class. If you have questions when you're trying for a baby and tracking ovulation , your doctor can provide answers and advice when it comes to when and how to use ovulation test strips.",
        "text_sha256": "221bc75145064687929d6d9c40d8534051922c574ca77797cee0787539bea7b4",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000059",
        "block_index": 59,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "And even if you feel twinges in your body that make you suspect there's a baby on board, don’t use an ovulation predictor kit to find out whether you're pregnant or not. Instead, wait until after your period is supposed to arrive and then check your urine with a home pregnancy test. Good luck!",
        "text_sha256": "a3e335ca7a3f8467ce4bfc5f97cc72c20523edd1eef6ae6a19c94d8833185b28",
        "word_count": 54
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000060",
        "block_index": 60,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Track your fertility with confidence. Download the What to Expect app and get personalized tips for every step of your TTC journey.",
        "text_sha256": "3e301ed27436a25cc471b6bc537380df37748c55810716b2ff08f33587897406",
        "word_count": 22
